{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T63WT4M5iyNQJX8579NaGf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd044-uname\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/uname: Print System Information\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts use uname to detect the operating system, kernel version, and hardware architecture\n6\t  at runtime. The utility supports individual flags for each information field and a combined\n7\t  flag (-a) that prints all fields. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n8\t  binary (guname, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit code, verified by\n9\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print system information fields matching guname output for all supported flags.\n13\t  - G2: Support the -a flag to print all fields in the canonical order.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Individual information flags\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the kernel name (equivalent to -s) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"-s must print the kernel name (e.g., Darwin, Linux).\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-n must print the network node hostname.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: \"-r must print the kernel release string.\"\n27\t      - R1.5:\n28\t          text: \"-v must print the kernel version string.\"\n29\t      - R1.6:\n30\t          text: \"-m must print the machine hardware name (e.g., x86_64, arm64).\"\n31\t      - R1.7:\n32\t          text: \"-p must print the processor type, or \\\"unknown\\\" if not determinable.\"\n33\t      - R1.8:\n34\t          text: \"-i must print the hardware platform, or \\\"unknown\\\" if not determinable.\"\n35\t      - R1.9:\n36\t          text: \"-o must print the operating system name.\"\n37\t\n38\t  R2:\n39\t    title: Combined output\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R2.1:\n42\t          text: \"-a must print all fields in the order: kernel name, node name, kernel release, kernel version, machine, processor, hardware platform, operating system, separated by single spaces.\"\n43\t      - R2.2:\n44\t          text: When multiple individual flags are specified (e.g., -sn), must print only the requested fields in the canonical order, space-separated, followed by a newline.\n45\t\n46\t  R3:\n47\t    title: Error handling\n48\t    items:\n49\t      - R3.1:\n50\t          text: Must not accept any positional operands. If an operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n51\t      - R3.2:\n52\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n53\t\n54\t  R4:\n55\t    title: Differential testing\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R4.1:\n58\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (guname) via pkg/testutils.\n59\t      - R4.2:\n60\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default (no flags), each individual flag (-s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p, -i, -o), -a, combinations of flags, and error cases.\"\n61\t      - R4.3:\n62\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n63\t\n64\tnon_goals:\n65\t  - cmd/uname does not set the hostname or any system information; it is read-only.\n66\t  - cmd/uname does not support long-form flag names beyond --help and --version.\n67\t\n68\tacceptance_criteria:\n69\t  - id: AC1\n70\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/uname prints the kernel name, matching guname.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R1.2\n74\t      - R1.3\n75\t      - R1.4\n76\t      - R1.5\n77\t      - R1.6\n78\t      - R1.7\n79\t      - R1.8\n80\t      - R1.9\n81\t  - id: AC2\n82\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/uname -a prints all fields in canonical order, matching guname.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R4.2\n86\t  - id: AC3\n87\t    criterion: \"Each individual flag (-s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p, -i, -o) produces output matching guname.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R1.1\n90\t      - R1.2\n91\t      - R1.3\n92\t      - R1.4\n93\t      - R1.5\n94\t      - R1.6\n95\t      - R1.7\n96\t      - R1.8\n97\t      - R1.9\n98\t      - R4.2\n99\t  - id: AC4\n100\t    criterion: \"Differential test against guname passes for all flag combinations and error cases.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R3.1\n103\t      - R3.2\n104\t      - R4.1\n105\t      - R4.2\n106\t      - R4.3\n107\t  - id: AC5\n108\t    criterion: \"cmd/uname compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n109\t    traces:\n110\t      - R1.1\n111\t      - R1.2\n112\t      - R1.3\n113\t      - R1.4\n114\t      - R1.5\n115\t      - R1.6\n116\t      - R1.7\n117\t      - R1.8\n118\t      - R1.9\n119\t      - R2.1\n120\t      - R2.2\n121\t      - R3.1\n122\t      - R3.2\n123\t      - R4.1\n124\t      - R4.2\n125\t      - R4.3\n126\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37e8a995-db88-465c-ac13-8aeb0f619c6d","uuid":"82edf5f2-54c5-4d63-b3bb-6d33d5e07100","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:40:06.829Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5198/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd044-uname.yaml","content":"id: srd044-uname\ntitle: \"cmd/uname: Print System Information\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts use uname to detect the operating system, kernel version, and hardware architecture\n  at runtime. The utility supports individual flags for each information field and a combined\n  flag (-a) that prints all fields. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (guname, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit code, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print system information fields matching guname output for all supported flags.\n  - G2: Support the -a flag to print all fields in the canonical order.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Individual information flags\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the kernel name (equivalent to -s) followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-s must print the kernel name (e.g., Darwin, Linux).\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-n must print the network node hostname.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-r must print the kernel release string.\"\n      - R1.5:\n          text: \"-v must print the kernel version string.\"\n      - R1.6:\n          text: \"-m must print the machine hardware name (e.g., x86_64, arm64).\"\n      - R1.7:\n          text: \"-p must print the processor type, or \\\"unknown\\\" if not determinable.\"\n      - R1.8:\n          text: \"-i must print the hardware platform, or \\\"unknown\\\" if not determinable.\"\n      - R1.9:\n          text: \"-o must print the operating system name.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Combined output\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-a must print all fields in the order: kernel name, node name, kernel release, kernel version, machine, processor, hardware platform, operating system, separated by single spaces.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: When multiple individual flags are specified (e.g., -sn), must print only the requested fields in the canonical order, space-separated, followed by a newline.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must not accept any positional operands. If an operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (guname) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: default (no flags), each individual flag (-s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p, -i, -o), -a, combinations of flags, and error cases.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/uname does not set the hostname or any system information; it is read-only.\n  - cmd/uname does not support long-form flag names beyond --help and --version.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/uname prints the kernel name, matching guname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n      - R1.8\n      - R1.9\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/uname -a prints all fields in canonical order, matching guname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Each individual flag (-s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p, -i, -o) produces output matching guname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n      - R1.8\n      - R1.9\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against guname passes for all flag combinations and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/uname compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n      - R1.8\n      - R1.9\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":126,"startLine":1,"totalLines":126}}}
